  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the probabilities of obtaining a favorable outcome (at least 2400 Euros). Lottery A has a 100% chance of a favorable outcome, while Lottery B has a 99% chance. Therefore, the reason would prefer A. However, in the verbal report, the individual does not mention the probability of a favorable outcome or compare these probabilities. Instead, the individual focuses on the 1% chance of getting nothing and the possibility of winning more (2500 Euros). This reflects a different reasoning—focusing on the risk of loss and the potential for a higher gain—rather than the rule of preferring the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. Since the individual does not apply the rule of the decision reason (comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes), the reason was not used. Thus, the individual did not use the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

